    <!-- Why rows -->
    <string name="why_next_break_rule">HeatShield counts work since your last break of 10 minutes or more, through each forecast hour\'s suggested rhythm, so rising heat or heavy work brings the next break forward. A shorter break pauses the count. Smoko or lunch within 15 minutes covers a due break. This is an app timer, not a measure of recovery.</string>
    <!-- The cadence Why row under the union table (C09): the same rows the panel and the break sheet use. -->
    <string name="why_cadence_union_rule">HeatShield\'s adaptation of VTHC\'s rest table, read on the peak\'s heat number with no personal adjustments: 45 min work then 15 min break from 30°, 30 then 30 from 32°, 15 then 45 from 34°, and from 36° stop work outdoors. Not the union\'s own rule.</string>
    <string name="why_cadence_union_none">The union table has no break row below a heat number of 30°.</string>
    <string name="why_next_break_union">HeatShield\'s adaptation of VTHC\'s rest table: the rows are read on the heat number with no personal adjustments, and HeatShield counts work since your last break of 10 minutes or more through each hour\'s row. From 36° the next step is to stop work outdoors, and nothing defers it. A shorter break pauses the count. This is an app timer, not a measure of recovery, and not the union\'s own rule.</string>

